{%- comment -%}
  Sets `season_of` to the name of the season a date falls in: the newest season
  that opened on or before it. `seasons:` in _data/mln.yml is ordered newest
  first, so the first match wins and no season needs an end date.

  The assign deliberately leaks to the caller — Jekyll includes share the page's
  scope — which is what lets the grid compare each week against the season it
  last printed a divider for. Read `season_of` immediately; the next include
  overwrites it.

  params: date ("%Y-%m-%d")
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign season_of = '' -%}
{%- for s in site.data.mln.seasons -%}
  {%- if season_of == '' and include.date >= s.start -%}
    {%- assign season_of = s.name -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
